{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#559","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#559","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#559\",\"parent_revision\":\"610b6569c7b115137787bbd4ea6b19600c404abd6d3f0e36c7c8abd0d021f22d\",\"root_revision\":\"610b6569c7b115137787bbd4ea6b19600c404abd6d3f0e36c7c8abd0d021f22d\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nClaim: \\\"plugin_validator.py validates structural concerns \u2026 does not scan for security risks\\\"\\n- VERIFIED. plugin_validator.py FrontmatterValidator (line 1849) checks are structural only. Zero matches for subprocess.call, os.system, eval(, exec( in plugin-creator validation scripts.\\n- SOURCE: plugins/plugin-creator/scripts/ (read 2026-04-15)\\n\\nClaim: \\\"No security-focused validation exists anywhere in the plugin-creator pipeline\\\"\\n- VERIFIED. skilllint error codes cover FM, SK, LK, PD, PL, NR, SL categories only \u2014 no SEC* codes exist.\\n- SOURCE: plugins/plugin-creator/docs/ERROR_CODES.md (read 2026-04-15)\\n\\nClaim: \\\"A scripts/skill_security_auditor.py script scans skill packages\\\"\\n- NOT YET IMPLEMENTED. No such script exists in plugins/plugin-creator/scripts/. This is the desired target state, not current state.\\n- SOURCE: Glob of plugins/plugin-creator/scripts/*.py confirmed absent (2026-04-15)\\n\\nClaim: plugin_validator.py described as if it exists and runs validation\\n- VERIFIED WITH NUANCE. File IS active \u2014 not removed. CLAUDE.md saying \\\"Removed \u2014 replaced by uvx skilllint@latest check\\\" is a documentation inaccuracy confirmed by item #1129 fact-check (status:verified). FrontmatterValidator at line 1849, active callers at lines 2098 and 4759, CLI entrypoint at line 5134.\\n- SOURCE: /root/.dh/projects/-home-user-claude_skills/backlog/p2-migrate-pluginvalidatorpy-to-delegate-frontmatter-validation.yaml (read 2026-04-15)\\n\\nExternal reference: skill-security-auditor exists in alirezarezvani/claude-skills v2.0.0+. Scans command injection, code execution, data exfiltration, prompt injection, supply chain risks, privilege escalation. Returns PASS/WARN/FAIL with remediation guidance. Stdlib-only Python, zero dependencies.\\n- VERIFIED (external). SOURCE: research/skill-generation-tools/claude-code-skills-alirezarezvani.md lines 260-283 (read 2026-04-15)\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nStatus: APPROVED-WITH-GAPS\\n\\nFunctional intent: AVAILABLE \u2014 four scan categories defined; PASS/WARN/FAIL verdict levels specified.\\nScope boundaries: AVAILABLE \u2014 in-scope: security scanning of skill packages; out-of-scope: structural validation (skilllint).\\nExternal interfaces: PARTIAL \u2014 test subject path known; delivery vehicle ambiguous (see Blockers).\\nConstraints: PARTIAL \u2014 exit codes defined (0/1/2); Python stdlib-only preferred per reference implementation.\\nExisting system context: AVAILABLE WITH GAPS \u2014 plugin_validator.py exists and is active; item #1129 (status:verified) is migrating it to delegate to skilllint.\\nVerification expectations: AVAILABLE \u2014 measurable signal defines test command and expected output.\\n\\nGap 1: Delivery vehicle not settled. Item assumes standalone script but item #1129 is migrating plugin_validator.py to delegate to skilllint. Extending plugin_validator.py now risks merge conflict with that verified migration work.\\nGap 2: allowed-tools deny-list of dangerous tool combinations is not defined in the codebase.\\nGap 3: No corpus of known-bad hook command patterns (pipe chains, external URL calls) exists locally to anchor the hook-injection check.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-15)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n7/10 \u2014 Security scanning is absent from the marketplace pipeline. Skills can contain prompt injection, exfiltration hooks, or over-granted tools today with no automated detection. P1 is appropriate given that marketplace exposure compounds the risk surface over time.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: Marketplace-scale skill distribution without a security gate. Skills installed from external marketplaces receive no pre-activation security vetting.\\n- Bottleneck: Plugin-creator pipeline has structural validation (skilllint) but zero security validation. Every plugin published today bypasses this gate.\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Automated detection of prompt injection patterns in SKILL.md body text before installation\\n- Detection of shell injection vectors in hook commands and allowed-tools frontmatter\\n- Static analysis of scripts/ files for dangerous Python patterns (eval, exec, os.system, subprocess.call(shell=True))\\n- PASS/WARN/FAIL verdict integrates into pre-commit and CI pipelines\\n- Fills the only unaddressed category in the plugin-creator quality pipeline\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen run against a skill package directory, the auditor scans all files without executing any of them. It reports a structured verdict with category-level findings. Exit code signals the overall verdict so CI pipelines can gate on it. Each finding includes file, line number, category, severity, and remediation text.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nA Python script at plugins/plugin-creator/scripts/skill_security_auditor.py (or equivalent delivery path) that accepts a skill package path, scans the four defined categories (scripts/ files for dangerous call patterns, hook commands for injection vectors, SKILL.md body for prompt injection markers, allowed-tools field against a deny-list), outputs structured findings with per-finding severity, exits 0/1/2 for PASS/WARN/FAIL, and requires no external dependencies beyond Python stdlib.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. Running the auditor against plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/ produces output containing a PASS/WARN/FAIL verdict and a findings list\\n2. Script exits 0 on a clean skill, 1 on warnings, 2 on failures\\n3. All four scan categories (scripts, hook commands, SKILL.md body, allowed-tools) present in output\\n4. Script runs without installing any packages beyond the Python stdlib\\n5. A skill containing os.system() in its scripts/ directory triggers at minimum a WARN finding\\n6. A SKILL.md body containing \\\"ignore previous instructions\\\" triggers at minimum a WARN finding\\n7. A skill with allowed-tools: Bash(*) without constraints triggers at minimum a WARN finding\\n8. Script produces no false positives against plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/ or documents known findings with rationale\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Prior work | plugins/plugin-creator/scripts/plugin_validator.py \u2014 existing validation pipeline (lines 1849, 4759) |\\n| Prior work | plugins/plugin-creator/docs/ERROR_CODES.md \u2014 existing error code taxonomy |\\n| Prior work | plugins/plugin-creator/scripts/frontmatter_core.py \u2014 Pydantic models for allowed-tools field (lines 88, 129) |\\n| External reference | alirezarezvani/claude-skills skill-security-auditor \u2014 stdlib-only Python reference implementation |\\n| Research | research/skill-generation-tools/claude-code-skills-alirezarezvani.md lines 260-283 |\\n| Agent | @plugin-creator:plugin-assessor |\\n| Skill | /plugin-creator:lint |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: Delivery vehicle decision (see Questions for Human). If option (b) extending plugin_validator.py is chosen, coordinate with item #1129 to avoid conflicting with its migration work.\\n- Blocks: None known. This is a new greenfield capability.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nMedium \u2014 Reference implementation in alirezarezvani/claude-skills provides a proven pattern. Core scanning logic for the four categories is straightforward static analysis (regex + AST parsing). Unknowns: (1) defining the deny-list for allowed-tools combinations, (2) resolving the delivery vehicle question. With those answered, implementation is approximately 1-2 days of focused work.\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\n- Delivery vehicle decision required before implementation begins. Extending plugin_validator.py while item #1129 migrates it to delegate to skilllint creates merge conflict risk.\\n- allowed-tools deny-list must be authored before the privilege escalation check can be implemented. No such list exists in the codebase.\\n\\n### Questions for Human\\n\\n- What is the intended delivery vehicle? Options: (a) standalone scripts/skill_security_auditor.py invoked independently; (b) new validator pass in plugin_validator.py alongside current validators; (c) contribution to skilllint as a new SEC* error code family. Note: Item #1129 (status:verified) is migrating plugin_validator.py to delegate to skilllint \u2014 option (b) may be obsoleted by that work.\\n- What constitutes FAIL vs WARN for allowed-tools? Is Bash(*) always FAIL, or only WARN unless combined with other risk signals? A deny-list must be defined before implementation.\\n- Should the auditor check only scripts/*.py files, or all files in the skill package including references/*.md for embedded code blocks?\\n- Should hooks/hooks.json be scanned for hook command patterns in addition to frontmatter allowed-tools?\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRun: `uv run plugins/plugin-creator/scripts/skill_security_auditor.py plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/` -- output includes a verdict (PASS/WARN/FAIL) and a findings list. Script exits 0 on PASS, 1 on WARN, 2 on FAIL. At least the four scan categories above are present in the output JSON.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **pre-activation skill security auditor for marketplace skills** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/skill-generation-tools/claude-code-skills-alirezarezvani.md -- pattern: skill-security-auditor scanning before activation\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-10\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`plugin_validator.py` validates structural concerns: YAML frontmatter schema, token complexity, internal link validity, plugin.json compliance, and progressive disclosure structure. It does not scan skill content for security risks such as command injection patterns in scripts, data exfiltration vectors in hook commands, prompt injection in SKILL.md body text, or privilege escalation via `allowed-tools` overgrants. No security-focused validation exists anywhere in the plugin-creator pipeline.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nA `scripts/skill_security_auditor.py` script (or new validator pass in `plugin_validator.py`) scans skill packages before marketplace publication or installation. Checks include: (1) scripts/ files scanned for `subprocess.call(shell=True)`, `os.system()`, `eval()`, `exec()` patterns; (2) hook commands in frontmatter checked for shell injection vectors (unquoted variables, pipe chains to external URLs); (3) SKILL.md body checked for prompt injection markers (instructions to ignore previous instructions, hidden system prompts); (4) `allowed-tools` field checked against a deny-list of dangerous tool combinations (e.g., `Bash(*)` without constraints). Each finding classified as PASS/WARN/FAIL with remediation text.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"f0c1604495dc94c01e66a5b10513e563c0e2c99c6989bc90b82e6e87c41b77f5\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPTD5Og\"}"}